{"obs_mqv8qj1r_b6cca377b580":{"observation":{"concepts":["system architecture","information retrieval"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User is requesting information regarding the architectural designs of 'xnch' and 'nexi'"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8qj1r_b6cca377b580","importance":2,"narrative":"The user initiated a recall command to access previously stored information regarding the architectural patterns and structural details of the XNCH and NEXI systems. This is a retrieval-oriented task to provide context for subsequent development or analysis.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"User query to retrieve architectural information for XNCH and NEXI","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:36.921Z","title":"Recall Request: XNCH and NEXI Architecture","type":"conversation"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8qn3t_1bd851c4194f":{"observation":{"concepts":["tool registry search","memory smart search"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Found match for 'mcp__plugin_agentmemory_agentmemory__memory_smart_search'","Total deferred tools in registry: 261"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8qn3t_1bd851c4194f","importance":3,"narrative":"The system performed a targeted search within the tool registry to locate the specific memory smart search tool. This is part of navigating the available toolset for the agent.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Querying tool registry for specific memory search functionality","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:42.145Z","title":"Search for memory smart search tool","type":"search"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8qtse_5add5a12287a":{"observation":{"concepts":["system logging","temporal tracking"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Current system timestamp recorded as 2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8qtse_5add5a12287a","importance":1,"narrative":"A system notification was received containing a specific timestamp. This serves as a temporal marker for the ongoing session.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Log entry for 2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z","title":"System Timestamp Notification","type":"notification"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8r7ae_35b323995dd4":{"observation":{"concepts":["graph extraction","code review initialization","duplicate edge prevention"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Retrieved several low-confidence lessons related to \"auto-import\" and code behavior.","Found relevant task: \"Code Review Initialization: XNCH/Nexi Platform\".","Retrieved notes about graph extraction issues (duplicate edges) and potential empty return values in existing logic."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8r7ae_35b323995dd4","importance":2,"narrative":"Executed a semantic search in the memory agent to find architectural context for XNCH and Nexi. The search returned fragmented lessons regarding specific coding patterns and a recent task for a platform code review.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Querying historical lessons and observations regarding XNCH/Nexi platform","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:08.325Z","title":"Memory search for XNCH and Nexi architecture","type":"search"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8re10_5a3ec7e014ab":{"observation":{"concepts":["architecture planning","pipeline discovery","semantic search"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Search query targeted \"xnch nexi architecture plan phases pipeline\"","Retrieved historical observations including task list updates, git diff summaries, and project file structure discovery","Identified relevant historical sessions related to XNCH/Nexi Platform code review initialization"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8re10_5a3ec7e014ab","importance":3,"narrative":"Performed a semantic search across the memory agent to retrieve context regarding the XNCH Nexi architecture plan. The search returned several related historical observations including project structure discovery and recent changes.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Querying historical observations for architecture phases and pipelines","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:17.079Z","title":"Memory search for XNCH Nexi architecture plan","type":"search"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8re79_2aa69a6b2830":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8re79_2aa69a6b2830","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"---\nname: user-ck-san\ndescription: \"User profile — ck-san, homelab AI builder targeting FDE/AI infrastructure roles\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: user\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\n---\n\nck-san is building XNCH/Nexi as a portfolio-grade AI infrastructure system and for personal use. Background includes PCI DSS / Rakuten experience. Targeting FDE (Founding/Senior/Principal Engineer) and AI infrastructure roles.\n\n**Technical depth:** Comfortable with distributed systems, k8s, Python async, FastAPI, PostgreSQL. Has thought deeply about AI architecture (brain-to-stack mapping, memory decay, perception hierarchies). Not an ML researcher — systems engineer who orchestrates AI.\n\n**Preferred collaboration style:**\n- Values architecture-first thinking over premature implementation\n- Wants to use OSS components and wire them together rather than reinventing\n- Prefers progressive enhancement: ship MVP fast, replace internals with owned IP over time\n- Thinks in phases (sees the full roadmap, executes sequentially)\n\n**System details:**\n- i7 node: control plane + memory (GTX 1650)\n- i9 node: inference (RTX 3090, Gemma 4 26B)\n- k8s already running on both nodes\n- Uses Obsidian vault as knowledge base\n- Plans: Telegram/WhatsApp as Nexi interface via OpenClaw\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:17.300Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"---\nname: user-ck-san\ndescription: \"User profile — ck-san, homelab AI builder targeting FDE/AI infrastructure roles\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: user\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\n---\n\nck-san is building XNCH/Nexi as a portfolio-grade AI infrastructure system and for personal use. Background includes PCI DSS / Rakuten experience. Targeting FDE (Founding/Senior/Principal Engineer) and AI infrastructure roles.\n\n**Technical depth:** Comfortable with distributed systems, k8s, Python async, FastAPI, PostgreSQL. Has thought deeply about AI architecture (brain-to-stack mapping, memory decay, perception hierarchies). Not an ML researcher — systems engineer who orchestrates AI.\n\n**Preferred collaboration style:**\n- Values architecture-first thinking over premature implementation\n- Wants to use OSS components and wire them together rather than reinventing\n- Prefers progressive enhancement: ship MVP fast, replace internals with owned IP over time\n- Thinks in phases (sees the full roadmap, executes sequentially)\n\n**System details:**\n- i7 node: control plane + memory (GTX 1650)\n- i9 node: inference (RTX 3090, Gemma 4 26B)\n- k8s already running on both nodes\n- Uses Obsidian vault as knowledge base\n- Plans: Telegram/WhatsApp as Nexi interface via OpenClaw\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8re79_1fc9ee3c1bdc":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8re79_1fc9ee3c1bdc","raw":{"tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md"},"tool_name":"Read","tool_output":{"file":{"content":"---\nname: project-xnch-nexi\ndescription: \"Core architecture context for the XNCH/Nexi homelab AI system — what it is, what exists, what's planned\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\n---\n\nXNCH is a private AI orchestration platform (routing + memory + perception + observability). Nexi is the product face (OpenClaw interface wired to XNCH). They run on a 2-node homelab k8s cluster.\n\n**Why:** ck-san is building this as a portfolio piece and personal AI system. Long-term goal: FDE/AI infrastructure interviews. The architecture demonstrates systems thinking over ML research.\n\n**Hardware:**\n- i7 + GTX 1650 4GB + 16GB RAM = Memory Node (xnch control plane, Redis, PostgreSQL+pgvector, Kuzu, LiteLLM, perception)\n- i9 + RTX 3090 24GB + 48GB RAM = Inference Node (Gemma 4 26B via vLLM, nexi decision engine, Mem0, Zep, OpenClaw)\n\n**Current codebase state (~65% complete):**\n- `xnch/` — governance/policy/memory/auth control plane. All 9 routes exist. Auth, episodic store (SQLite), policy engine, audit JSONL all working.\n- `nexi/` — decision pipeline (intent → options → policy filter → score → verdict → dispatch). Evaluator and selector solid; intent_interpreter, option_generator, plan_compiler are stubs.\n- `xnch/learning/` — pattern_extractor, score_adapter, policy_candidates all stubs.\n- No Docker/k8s files, no LiteLLM, no pgvector, no Kuzu, no Langfuse, no perception.\n\n**Approved master plan:** `/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md`\n\n**Execution sequence:** Phase 0 (fix 4 critical gaps) → Phase 1 (XnchMemory pgvector+Kuzu) → Phase 2 (LiteLLM routing) → Phase 3 (intent interpreter real impl) → Phase 6 (OpenClaw → Nexi live) → Phase 5 (Langfuse) → Phase 4 (perception) → Phase 7 (learning loop) → Phase 8 (k8s manifests)\n\n**How to apply:** Always consult the plan file before implementing. Phase 0 must complete before any other phase. After Phase 6, Nexi is live — everything after is progressive enhancement.\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29},"type":"text"}},"sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:17.300Z","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md"},"toolName":"Read","toolOutput":{"file":{"content":"---\nname: project-xnch-nexi\ndescription: \"Core architecture context for the XNCH/Nexi homelab AI system — what it is, what exists, what's planned\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\n---\n\nXNCH is a private AI orchestration platform (routing + memory + perception + observability). Nexi is the product face (OpenClaw interface wired to XNCH). They run on a 2-node homelab k8s cluster.\n\n**Why:** ck-san is building this as a portfolio piece and personal AI system. Long-term goal: FDE/AI infrastructure interviews. The architecture demonstrates systems thinking over ML research.\n\n**Hardware:**\n- i7 + GTX 1650 4GB + 16GB RAM = Memory Node (xnch control plane, Redis, PostgreSQL+pgvector, Kuzu, LiteLLM, perception)\n- i9 + RTX 3090 24GB + 48GB RAM = Inference Node (Gemma 4 26B via vLLM, nexi decision engine, Mem0, Zep, OpenClaw)\n\n**Current codebase state (~65% complete):**\n- `xnch/` — governance/policy/memory/auth control plane. All 9 routes exist. Auth, episodic store (SQLite), policy engine, audit JSONL all working.\n- `nexi/` — decision pipeline (intent → options → policy filter → score → verdict → dispatch). Evaluator and selector solid; intent_interpreter, option_generator, plan_compiler are stubs.\n- `xnch/learning/` — pattern_extractor, score_adapter, policy_candidates all stubs.\n- No Docker/k8s files, no LiteLLM, no pgvector, no Kuzu, no Langfuse, no perception.\n\n**Approved master plan:** `/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md`\n\n**Execution sequence:** Phase 0 (fix 4 critical gaps) → Phase 1 (XnchMemory pgvector+Kuzu) → Phase 2 (LiteLLM routing) → Phase 3 (intent interpreter real impl) → Phase 6 (OpenClaw → Nexi live) → Phase 5 (Langfuse) → Phase 4 (perception) → Phase 7 (learning loop) → Phase 8 (k8s manifests)\n\n**How to apply:** Always consult the plan file before implementing. Phase 0 must complete before any other phase. After Phase 6, Nexi is live — everything after is progressive enhancement.\n","filePath":"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29},"type":"text"}},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8rjbp_6ea4caad981e":{"observation":{"concepts":["Multi-layer memory architecture","Hierarchical storage (Redis, PostgreSQL, Kuzu)","Inference routing proxy","Distributed hardware assignment"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Current system implements ~65% of governance/decision core","Critical naming collision: XNCH (platform) vs Nexi (product interface)","Identified 4 critical gaps (C-1 to C-4) regarding scoring dimensions, DAG schema, DSL enums, and pattern extractor grouping","Architecture requires migration from SQLite to PostgreSQL/pgvector for Layer 2 memory","Hardware split: i7 node for memory/control plane, i9 node for inference (vLLM/Gemma 4)"],"files":["/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md"],"id":"obs_mqv8rjbp_6ea4caad981e","importance":7,"narrative":"Read the master architecture plan to understand the roadmap for completing the XNCH/Nexi system, including the transition from SQLite to a more robust memory hierarchy and the distinction between the XNCH platform and the Nexi product layer.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Reviewing XNCH/Nexi end-to-end architecture plan","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:23.946Z","title":"Read architecture plan","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8rvl0_7c43f614a95f":{"observation":{"concepts":[],"confidence":0.75,"facts":["The subagent has finished its assigned task"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8rvl0_7c43f614a95f","importance":1,"narrative":"The subagent was stopped, indicating that the specific task or sub-process it was managing has reached a terminal state. This signifies a transition back to the primary agent's control.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Termination of subagent process","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:05:39.833Z","title":"Subagent execution completed","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8u0ag_100447887520":{"observation":{"concepts":["git history","branch management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["HEAD is at commit 29079db (v0)","Recent branches include v4-localOC and v3","Commit 43ad614 (v2) contained docs update","Initial commit is 984b095 (main)"],"files":["nexi/"],"id":"obs_mqv8u0ag_100447887520","importance":2,"narrative":"The user executed a git log command to inspect the commit history of the nexi directory. This reveals the current branch state and recent development activity within that subdirectory.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Checking recent commit history in nexi/ folder","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:19.244Z","title":"Git log for nexi directory","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8u0se_420c491ae22b":{"observation":{"concepts":["fallback chain","rule-based templates","intent-based action specs","model adapter pattern"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The nexi/ directory was recently initialized with new files.","ModelAdapter implements a 4-stage fallback chain: vllm-primary, vllms-secondary, llama-cpp-python, and rule-based templates.","Rule-based templates define specific action types (READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, etc.) for different IntentClasses (QUERY, DECISION, EXECUTION).","New package structure includes nexi/__init__.py, nexi/adapters/__init__.py, and nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py."],"files":["nexi/nexi/__init__.py","nexi/nexi/adapters/__init__.py","nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8u0se_420c491ae22b","importance":6,"narrative":"The git diff shows the initial creation of the Nexi decision engine. It introduces a multi-layered model adapter with a fallback mechanism and a rule-based template system for handling different intent classes.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Reviewing recent changes to the nexi/ directory","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:19.885Z","title":"New commit: Initialization of Nexi project","type":"discovery"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8u68j_698a31d7c038":{"observation":{"concepts":["LiteLLM proxy integration","Dynamic request routing","Model fallback patterns","Inference abstraction"],"confidence":1,"facts":["ModelAdapter is transitioning from a hardcoded vllm-primary/secondary fallback chain to a LiteLLM proxy-based approach.","Introduced `classify_request` from `xnch.routing.classifier` to determine model routing.","Refactored `_call_vllm` to `_call_litellm` which accepts a specific `model_name` derived from request classification.","Updated fallback chain to use `litellm_proxy_url` and `litellm_proxy_timeout_s` from settings."],"files":["nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py","nexi/nexi/config.py","nexi/nexi/main.py","nexi/nexi/models/__init__.py","nexi/nexi/models/intent.py","nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py","nexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py","nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py","nexi/nexi/utils/audit.py","nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8u68j_698a31d7c038","importance":7,"narrative":"The git diff shows a significant architectural shift in how the ModelAdapter handles inference requests, moving from a static multi-stage fallback chain to a dynamic routing system using LiteLLM and a request classifier. This change introduces more flexibility by allowing request-specific model selection via a routing agent.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Reviewing modifications to model adapter and routing logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:26.950Z","title":"Git diff of unstaged changes in nexi codebase","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8ua51_59d7b5905165":{"observation":{"concepts":["LiteLLM proxy","request routing","LLM observability","dynamic model selection"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Modified nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py to replace direct vLLM calls with a LiteLLM proxy approach.","Introduced `classify_request` from `xnch.routing.classifier` to determine model route based on input.","Added `trace_llm_call` from `xnch.observability.langfuse_client` for observability.","Deprecated the explicit multi-step vLLM fallback chain in favor of a unified LiteLLM endpoint usage.","The `_call_litellm` method now accepts a dynamic `model_name` determined by the classifier."],"files":["nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8ua51_59d7b5905165","importance":7,"narrative":"The ModelAdapter has been refactored to use a LiteLLM proxy instead of a manually managed vLLM fallback chain. This change introduces request classification to dynamically route prompts to appropriate models and adds observability via Langfuse.","sessionId":"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0","subtitle":"Migrating from hardcoded vLLM chain to LiteLLM proxy with dynamic routing","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:32.008Z","title":"Refactor ModelAdapter to use LiteLLM and Request Classification","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8ubxt_295a0e30ad51":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8ubxt_295a0e30ad51","raw":{"tool_input":{"command":"git diff HEAD --name-only -- nexi/","description":"List changed nexi files only"},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":{"interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"stderr":"","stdout":"nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\nnexi/nexi/config.py\nnexi/nexi/main.py\nnexi/nexi/models/__init__.py\nnexi/nexi/models/intent.py\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\nnexi/nexi/utils/audit.py\nnexi/tests/test_